            <ArticleTitle>Obturator externus pyomyositis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>638-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000000212</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pyomyositis of the obturator externus muscle is a rare cause of limp and hip pain in children. The exact etiology of the condition remains poorly understood, although a mechanism of transient bacteremia in association with increased muscle susceptibility has been proposed. This case describes the course of a rather than 1 child from presentation to diagnosis and demonstrates the requirement for magnetic resonance imaging in establishing a diagnosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
